<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roda de Isábena</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roda de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabena">Isábena</a> is a small hilltop village in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huesca">Huesca</a>, Aragon, in the valley of the Isábena. In the 10th century the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ribagorza">Ribagorza</a> made it the seat of a bishopric, and its Romanesque cathedral of San Vicente, among the oldest in Aragon, still stands. The see was moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> after that city's conquest in 1149.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roda-de-isabena.jpg" alt="Roda de Isábena" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mmorell · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roda-de-isabena-palacio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
